The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (bp->flags & BNXT_FLAG_AGG_RINGS)
    rx_rings <<= 1;
```
```c
_bnxt_get_max_rings(bp, &max_rx, &max_tx, &max_cp);
```
```c
if (max_rx < rx_rings)
    return -ENOMEM;
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the adjustment for AGG rings is made before calling `_bnxt_get_max_rings()`, which already accounts for AGG rings. This results in the `rx_rings` being effectively doubled before the maximum number of rings is determined, leading to a situation where the validation check for `max_rx` may fail due to an inflated `rx_rings` value.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
_bnxt_get_max_rings(bp, &max_rx, &max_tx, &max_cp);
```
```c
if (bp->flags & BNXT_FLAG_AGG_RINGS)
    rx_rings <<= 1;
```
Reason:
The fix involves moving the adjustment for `rx_rings` after the call to `_bnxt_get_max_rings()`. This ensures that the maximum number of rings is calculated correctly without the premature doubling of `rx_rings`, thus preventing the potential failure in the validation check for available rings.

